Article 35 Under any of the following circumstances, the tax authority has the power to assess the taxpayer's tax payable:
(1) The taxpayer may, in accordance with the provisions of laws and administrative regulations, maintain no accounting books;
(2) The taxpayer shall, in accordance with the provisions of laws and administrative regulations, maintain accounting books but fails to do so;
(3) The taxpayer has destroyed accounting books without authorization or refuses to provide tax payment materials;
(4) The taxpayer maintains accounting books, but the accounts are confused, or the cost materials, income vouchers, and expense vouchers are incomplete, making it difficult to audit the accounts;
(5) The taxpayer, having incurred tax liability, fails to file tax returns within the prescribed time limit and, after being ordered by the tax authority to file within a time limit, still fails to do so within the extended time limit;
(6) The tax basis declared by the taxpayer is obviously low and without justifiable reasons.
The specific procedures and methods for assessing tax payable by tax authorities shall be prescribed by the State Council's tax authority.

Article 54 The tax authorities shall have the authority to conduct the following tax inspections:
(1) To inspect a taxpayer's account books, vouchers, statements and relevant information, and to inspect a withholding agent's account books, vouchers and relevant information concerning the taxes withheld or collected;
(2) To inspect a taxpayer's taxable commodities, goods or other property at the taxpayer's production or business premises and places where goods are stored, and to inspect a withholding agent's business operations relevant to the withholding or collection of taxes;
(3) To order a taxpayer or withholding agent to provide documents, evidentiary materials and relevant information relating to the payment of taxes or the withholding or collection of taxes;
(4) To inquire of a taxpayer or withholding agent questions and circumstances relating to the payment of taxes or the withholding or collection of taxes;
(5) To inspect, at railway stations, docks, airports, postal enterprises and their branches, the relevant documents, vouchers and materials relating to the taxable commodities, goods or other property transported or mailed by a taxpayer;
(6) With the approval of the director of a tax bureau (or its branch) at or above the county level, and by presenting a permit for inspecting deposit accounts in a nationally unified form, to inquire about the deposit accounts of a taxpayer engaged in production or business operations, or a withholding agent, at banks or other financial institutions. When investigating tax-related illegal cases, the tax authorities may, with the approval of the director of a tax bureau (or its branch) at or above the level of a city divided into districts or an autonomous prefecture, inquire about the savings deposits of persons suspected of being involved in the case. The materials obtained by the tax authorities through inquiry shall not be used for purposes other than taxation.

Article 60 Where a taxpayer commits any of the following acts, the tax authorities shall order the taxpayer to make corrections within a prescribed time limit and may impose a fine of not more than 2,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, a fine of not less than 2,000 yuan but not more than 10,000 yuan shall be imposed:
(1) Failing to apply for, change or cancel tax registration within the prescribed time limit;
(2) Failing to set up or keep account books, or to keep the vouchers and relevant materials, in accordance with the provisions;
(3) Failing to submit the financial and accounting systems or methods of financial and accounting treatment, and the accounting software, to the tax authorities for record, in accordance with the provisions;
(4) Failing to report all of the taxpayer's bank account numbers to the tax authorities, in accordance with the provisions;
(5) Failing to install or use the tax control devices, or damaging or making unauthorized changes to such devices, in accordance with the provisions.
Where a taxpayer fails to undergo tax registration, the tax authorities shall order the taxpayer to make corrections within a prescribed time limit; if the taxpayer fails to do so within the prescribed time limit, upon the request of the tax authorities, the administrative department for industry and commerce shall revoke the taxpayer's business license.
Where a taxpayer fails to use the tax registration certificate in accordance with the provisions, or lends, alters, damages, sells or forges the tax registration certificate, a fine of not less than 2,000 yuan but not more than 10,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 50,000 yuan shall be imposed.
